# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need. run_experiment.py loads .env
# at start-up; variables already exported in your shell take precedence. .env is
# gitignored — never commit real credentials.

# --- Model access ------------------------------------------------------------
# The shipped config.toml uses provider = "openai" with model = "gpt-5.5", so
# this is the one value most setups need. Uncomment it and paste your key.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# For provider = "anthropic" in config.toml
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# For a custom endpoint / evaluation relay: whatever variable name you declared
# as "apiKey" in pi-agent/models.json (see README "Model access")
# TRACES_EPISODE_TOKEN=

# Login-based providers (e.g. provider = "openai-codex") use a stored login
# rather than a key, and pi keeps that login in its agent directory. The runner
# points the agent directory at the repo-local pi-agent/ unless this is set, so
# such a provider needs the directory that holds the login:
# PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR=/absolute/path/to/.pi/agent

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The practice environments, if they are not in ./vendor or next to this repo
# EW_EXAMPLES_REPO=/absolute/path/to/executable-world-examples

# A pi executable other than ./node_modules/.bin/pi
# PI_BIN=/absolute/path/to/pi

# Extension pack switches are NOT set here: config.toml [run.guards] is the only
# place they are configured, and the runner injects every one of them explicitly
# into each episode (the eight core rules and the writing-protocol pack on, the
# phase mechanism off), so an EW_GUARD_* left in a shell cannot change a run.
